## CoalesceBatchesExec with fetch
  case default:
    CoalesceBatchesExec: target_batch_size=8192, fetch=10
      MockSourceExec: partitioning=UnknownPartitioning(3), partition_rows=[200, 0, 400], statistics=Exact
    [invariant] fetch_not_equal_cardinality at CoalesceBatchesExec (root): fetch() is Some(10), but cardinality_effect() is Equal; a fetch can drop input rows, so the effect should be LowerEqual while a fetch is set
    [lint] limit_pushdown_missed at CoalesceBatchesExec (root): supports_limit_pushdown() is false, but with every child limited to its first n rows per partition, for n in [1, 7, 601], every output partition has the first n rows of the same partition of the normal output, so a limit above the node could be pushed to its children; return true from supports_limit_pushdown if this holds for every input
